from pathlib import Path
import csv,json
import numpy as np
import matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
rows=list(csv.DictReader((P/'enrichment_summary.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t'));d={r['metric']:r for r in rows};meta=json.loads((P/'analysis_metadata.json').read_text());N=meta['n_LARs']
keys=['LAR_any_interaction','LAR_one_hit_interaction','LAR_two_hit_interaction'];labels=['Any interaction','One-hit interaction','Two-hit interaction']
obs=np.array([float(d[k]['observed']) for k in keys])/N*100
means=np.array([float(d[k]['null_mean']) for k in keys])/N*100
low=np.array([float(d[k]['null_2_5_percentile']) for k in keys])/N*100
high=np.array([float(d[k]['null_97_5_percentile']) for k in keys])/N*100
fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(9,5));x=np.arange(3);ax.bar(x-.18,obs,.34,label='Observed LARs',color='#003f7f');ax.bar(x+.18,means,.34,yerr=[means-low,high-means],capsize=4,label='Shuffled mean (95% null interval)',color='#adb9c6')
for i,k in enumerate(keys):
 ax.text(i, max(obs[i],high[i])+3,f"{float(d[k]['fold_enrichment']):.3f}×; p = 0.001",ha='center',fontsize=10)
ax.set_xticks(x);ax.set_xticklabels(labels);ax.set_ylabel('Unique LARs (% of 28,688)');ax.set_ylim(0,105);ax.spines[['top','right']].set_visible(False);ax.legend(loc='lower left',bbox_to_anchor=(0,1.02),frameon=False);ax.set_title('LAR participation in HiCorr interactions',pad=42)
fig.text(.1,.015,'1,000 shuffles; chromosome and length preserved. One-hit and two-hit groups overlap.',fontsize=9,color='#555555');fig.tight_layout(rect=[0,.05,1,1]);fig.savefig(P/'LAR_HiCorr_enrichment.png',dpi=200);plt.close(fig)
lines=['# LAR–HiCorr overlap and shuffled enrichment','', '## Main result','',f'Of **{N:,} unique LARs**, **25,834 (90.05%)** overlap at least one interaction. This is **1.054-fold** the random expectation under the specified chromosome- and length-matched null.','', '| Unique-LAR measure | Observed | % of all LARs | Shuffled mean | 95% null interval | Fold enrichment | Empirical enrichment p |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for k,label in zip(keys,labels):
 r=d[k];lines.append(f"| {label} | {int(r['observed']):,} | {float(r['observed_percent_of_LARs']):.2f}% | {float(r['null_mean']):,.2f} | {float(r['null_2_5_percentile']):,.2f}–{float(r['null_97_5_percentile']):,.2f} | {float(r['fold_enrichment']):.3f} | {float(r['p_enrichment']):.6f} |")
lines += ['', 'The 95% null interval describes shuffled counts, not a confidence interval on the observed count or effect size.', '', '## Definitions and non-overlapping categories','', '- One-hit interaction: exactly one BEDPE anchor overlaps at least one LAR.', '- Two-hit interaction: both BEDPE anchors overlap at least one LAR. This does not require exactly two distinct LARs; an anchor can overlap multiple LARs, and the same LAR may overlap both anchors.', '- A unique LAR can participate in both interaction types. Therefore the one-hit and two-hit LAR totals must not be added.', '', '| Exclusive LAR category | Count |','|---|---:|','| Only one-hit interactions | 18,882 |','| Only two-hit interactions | 193 |','| Both interaction types | 6,759 |','| No interaction | 2,854 |','| Total | 28,688 |','', '## Interaction-row counts are a different endpoint','', '| Interaction type | Observed rows | Shuffled mean | Fold | Enrichment p | Depletion p |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for k,label in [('interactions_one_hit','One-hit'),('interactions_two_hit','Two-hit')]:
 r=d[k];lines.append(f"| {label} | {int(r['observed']):,} | {float(r['null_mean']):,.2f} | {float(r['fold_enrichment']):.3f} | {float(r['p_enrichment']):.6f} | {float(r['p_depletion']):.6f} |")
lines += ['', '**Two-hit interaction rows are not enriched** (p = 0.732), even though more unique LARs participate in them than expected. A different distribution of interactions across regions can produce these two findings. One-hit interaction rows are depleted under this null. Counts are BEDPE rows; any input duplicates remain represented.','', '## Methods','', '- Fixed interaction background: all 1,691,689 rows of Merged.raw_HiCorr_DeepLoop.1.5.bedpe, not just the LAR-filtered subset.', '- Observed intervals: all 28,688 uniquely named rows in pgls_LARs_hg19.bed; overlap uses coordinate columns 1–3, never coordinates embedded in the ID.', '- Overlap: at least 1 bp using hg19 0-based half-open coordinates. Merely touching boundaries is not an overlap.', '- 1,000 permutations; NumPy default_rng seed 20260918. Each region retains its original chromosome and exact length, with a start sampled uniformly from all in-bounds positions on that chromosome.', '- All original contigs are retained. The 248 LARs on contigs with no HiCorr anchors cannot overlap in either the observed or shuffled analysis.', '- Shuffled LARs may overlap each other and the observed regions. No gap, blacklist, mappability, accessibility, TSS-distance or local-clustering matching is applied.', '- For each shuffled set, recompute anchor overlap and one-hit/two-hit labels from scratch.', '- One-sided empirical enrichment p = (1 + number of shuffled counts >= observed)/(1 + 1,000); depletion uses <=. No normal approximation is used. Reported p-values are unadjusted. Zero exceedances yields 1/1001 = 0.000999, not zero.', '- Fold enrichment = observed count / mean shuffled count. The three primary LAR tests all had zero exceedances; finite permutation resolution limits precision.', '', '## Interpretation','', 'These results establish enrichment relative to uniform chromosome- and length-matched placements, not a specific regulatory mechanism. The enrichment is modest in magnitude despite small permutation p-values. A stricter background matched for assay detectability, accessibility or gene proximity may change the result. Shuffling also disrupts genomic clustering of the LARs.','', '## Validation and files','', 'Observed unique-LAR membership was independently checked against the prior annotated BEDPE. The classification algorithm matched a brute-force implementation on 100 synthetic interaction graphs.', '', '- `LAR_interaction_membership.tsv`: all LARs with one-hit/two-hit membership and exclusive category.', '- `enrichment_summary.tsv`: all observed counts, null summaries, folds, and empirical p-values.', '- `shuffle_counts.tsv`: results from every permutation.', '- `analysis_metadata.json`: seed, settings and SHA-256 input checksums.', '- `LAR_HiCorr_enrichment.png`: observed versus shuffled unique-LAR percentages.', '- `analyze.py`: reproducible analysis; run from any working directory with Python and NumPy.', '', 'Chromosome lengths: [UCSC hg19 chromosome sizes](https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/hg19/bigZips/hg19.chrom.sizes). Inputs and browser data were not modified.']
(P/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print(P/'REPORT.md')
